---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// Items marked TODO need a committee decision before launch; they are highlighted on the page.
const updated = '23 September 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy notice | CUDGS">
    <article>
        <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
        <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
            This website is run by the Cambridge University Digital Gaming Society (CUDGS), a student society.
            CUDGS is the data controller for the personal data described here. Contact the committee at
            <mark>TODO: society email address</mark>.
        </p>

        <h2>Logging in</h2>
        <p>
            You can log in with your University of Cambridge account. Logins go through Nevar, a service run by the
            Student-Run Computing Facility (SRCF). We receive only your CRSid and whether you are a current member of
            the University. We never see your password. SRCF's own privacy information is on srcf.net.
        </p>

        <h2>Membership records</h2>
        <p>
            For each member, the committee keeps your name, CRSid, membership type and the date your membership ends,
            in a private Google Sheet that only the committee and this website can read. When you log in, the website
            reads your row to show your membership and members-only content.
        </p>
        <p>
            We use this data to run your membership, which is part of our agreement with you (UK GDPR Article 6(1)(b)).
            We keep it until <mark>TODO: e.g. one year after your membership ends</mark>, then delete it.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
            When you log in we set one cookie, <code>cudgs_session</code>, which keeps you logged in for up to 7 days
            or until you log out. It contains your CRSid and a security signature, nothing else. It is strictly
            necessary for logging in, so it doesn't need your consent. We don't use analytics, advertising or
            tracking cookies.
        </p>

        <h2>Other services this site uses</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Hosting:</strong> the site is hosted by <mark>TODO: hosting provider</mark>, which keeps
                standard server logs (your IP address and the pages you request) for
                <mark>TODO: log retention period</mark> to keep the site secure.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Events list:</strong> loaded from Baserow (baserow.io, based in the EU). Your browser connects
                to Baserow directly, so Baserow sees your IP address. Event images may be loaded from other websites.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Google:</strong> stores the membership sheet. Google may process data outside the UK under the
                safeguards in its data processing terms.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Instagram and Discord:</strong> only if you follow our links; their own privacy policies apply.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p>We never sell your data or share it for marketing.</p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
            Under UK data protection law you can ask to see the data we hold about you, have it corrected or deleted,
            object to or restrict how we use it, or receive a copy. Contact the committee to do any of these. If you're
            unhappy with how we've handled your data, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at
            <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk</a> or on 0303 123 1113.
        </p>
    </article>
</Base>

<style>
    article {
        padding: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
        border-radius: 0.75rem;
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        line-height: 2;
        background: rgb(14 17 22 / 0.9);
    }

    h1 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 0.9rem + 1.5vw, 2rem);
        color: var(--cam-blue);
        text-shadow: 3px 3px 0 var(--cam-dark-blue);
    }

    h2 {
        margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        color: var(--cam-blue);
    }

    .updated {
        color: #B5BDC8;
    }

    p,
    ul {
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
    }

    li + li {
        margin-top: 0.5rem;
    }

    a {
        color: var(--cam-blue);
    }

    /* Highlights details the committee still has to fill in. */
    mark {
        padding: 0 0.3rem;
        color: var(--black);
        background: var(--cam-blue);
    }
</style>
